{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>ואבכה</b> — The [object] marker is [elided] from the verb, like: ולבכותה." "<b>ותהי</b> — As I mentioned, the force of the Name [HaShem] in a verb is either past or future, and so it is here: ואבכה — 'I wept' — became a reproach to me."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 69, :notes {1 "Resolved הזכרתי כי כח השם as referring to the divine name as vav-conversive marker; 'the Name' preserved per divine-names rule."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:24.837237512Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}